From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:47:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: mt6797: add the CONSYS I2S input

The FM receiver in the connectivity subsystem sends its audio as a 32
kHz, 16-bit I2S master into the AFE's second I2S input. The vendor
kernel takes it as a slave from the CONSYS pad and converts it with the
I2S ASRC to 44.1 or 48 kHz.

Add a CONNSYS_I2S capture DAI that does the same: AFE_I2S_CON as a
16-bit I2S slave from the CONSYS pad, the I2S block at the output rate
in AFE_DAC_CON1, and the vendor's ASRC settings, which are the constants
mainline MT8186 uses for its CONSYS I2S. The input clock (AUDIO_TOP_CON0
PDN_I2S) is a supply of the capture stream. Stopping bypasses the ASRC
again, as the vendor does.

The fields of AFE_I2S_CON, AFE_ASRC_CON0 and AFE_ASRC_CON13 are defined
in the new file as the vendor programs them; mt6797-reg.h does not name
them.
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/Makefile            |   3 +-
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-afe-common.h |   2 +
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-afe-pcm.c    |   1 +
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-dai-i2s.c    | 144 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 149 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-dai-i2s.c

